# 🪵 Lite log inspector 

A small beginner Linux project I made while learning log analysis.

It takes sample logs and uses basic Linux commands to pull out useful info like top IPs, failed logins, status codes, and suspicious activity.

---

## ⚡ What I used

`cp` • `chmod` • `grep` • `awk` • `sort` • `uniq` • `head` • `ps` • `ss` • `find`

---

## 📁 Files

- `access.log`
- `auth.log`
- `analysis.sh`
- `.gitignore`

---

## ▶️ Run

```bash
chmod +x analysis.sh
./analysis.sh
```

---

## 📤 Output

A `report/` folder is created with summary files.

---

## 📝 Note

This is a beginner project, so I kept the code simple and easy to read.